# Data (large files, regenerable)
data/raw/
data/processed/*
data/geodata/
data/cache/

# FORK-ONLY EXCEPTION, same reasoning as the reports/ one below. This CSV is
# derived, but it is NOT fully re-derivable: three rows are `source=manual`
# (ruv-483052, the Gallup/Áfram Ísland poll) because RÚV never tagged that
# article a poll, so `list` cannot see it and `fetch` cannot reach it. Rerunning
# the pipeline on an empty checkout silently produces a SMALLER file, and
# AGENTS.md tells readers to query this exact path with duckdb.
# It is 8 KB, and because rows are written sorted, a diff means something real:
# a number that moves is either an edited article or a changed extractor.
!data/processed/skodanakannanir.csv

# DuckDB
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.python-version
.uv/

# Playwright browsers
.playwright/

# Reports (self-contained HTML + one-off report scripts, local only)
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# FORK-ONLY EXCEPTION. The rule above is right for a one-off report: it is
# reproducible from the scripts and data that ARE tracked, so keeping it out of
# git costs nothing. The ESB set is not that. build_esb_report.py holds ~30 KB
# of numbers read by hand out of article prose, plus the editorial calls that
# go with them (which framing each poll measures, which basis, who commissioned
# it, why one poll is excluded). None of that can be regenerated by rerunning
# anything. It is also the source of truth for a page that is published and
# shared publicly, and updated repeatedly rather than written once.
# Untracked, it existed in exactly one place on one disk.
!reports/build_esb_report.py
!reports/esb_kannanir_2026.json
!reports/esb-kannanir-2026-artifact.html

# Claude plans
.claude/plans/

# Local Claude settings (machine-specific permission grants)
.claude/settings.local.json

# R
.Rhistory
.Rdata
.Rproj.user/

# Raw data downloads under non-standard paths
data/logbyli/

# Scratch metadata files written by scripts at runtime
metadata/maelabord-ctx*.txt

# Tesseract language data (downloaded on demand)
*.traineddata

